Reliability hardening rollout summary (May 2026)

Backend:
- Added strict validation shared helpers for text/lang/mode and upload media checks.
- Hardened LiteLLM integration with retries, bounded response decode, schema checks, and circuit breaker.
- Hardened OCR client with retry/backoff improvements, Retry-After support, bounded decode, and response schema validation.
- Added structured reliability logs for retry/circuit/rejection paths.
- Added in-memory reliability counters and exposed them from /api/v1/metrics/ocr.
- Persisted reliability events to Postgres via pglog handler.
- Added migrations:
  - 003_create_reliability_events.sql
  - 004_add_reliability_retention_policy.sql
- Added integration test coverage for pglog Postgres insert paths (skips unless LOKLINGO_TEST_POSTGRES_DSN is set).

Frontend:
- Added Reliability panel with live counters + windowed reliability event table.
- Added readiness-popover mini reliability widget with:
  - trend delta (up/down/flat)
  - rolling sparkline
  - quick jump to full Reliability panel
- Added severity thresholds with Vite env vars:
  - VITE_RELIABILITY_PRESSURE_WARN
  - VITE_RELIABILITY_PRESSURE_CRITICAL

Docs/ops:
- README updated with migration/apply steps, retention helper usage, metrics endpoint details, and threshold configuration.
- analytics/ocr_dashboard.sql extended with reliability trend/failure queries.

Validation status:
- backend: go test ./...
- frontend: npm run lint && npm run build
- All green after each hardening increment.

