OCR-only mode rollout summary (May 2026)

Backend:
- Added mode constant: `ocr_only`.
- Allowed `ocr_only` for image/PDF endpoints while keeping text endpoint modes unchanged.
- Worker behavior:
  - image + `ocr_only`: OCR extract only, no translation render, job completes with extracted text fields.
  - pdf + `ocr_only`: OCR pages extract only, no translation call, job completes with extracted text fields.
- Sync image endpoint now returns text/source/target and only includes image_url when output exists.

Frontend:
- Added mode option: OCR only (no translation).
- Image OCR-only flow now executes a single OCR request (no overlay/layout comparison fan-out).
- Added output badge to distinguish OCR extraction from translated text.
- PDF Jobs panel now stores and displays submitted mode, including an OCR-only pill per queued job.

Validation status:
- backend: go test ./...
- frontend: npm run lint && npm run build
- All green for OCR-only changes.

---

Hardening increment (queue safety + upload signature checks)

Backend:
- Redis queue processing hardened with inflight bookkeeping:
  - dequeue now atomically moves IDs from queue -> inflight
  - worker acks inflight IDs after processing
  - stale inflight IDs are periodically recovered back to the queue
- Upload validation now verifies file signatures (magic bytes):
  - PDF requires `%PDF-` header
  - image uploads validate PNG/JPEG/GIF/WEBP signatures and extension match
- Size-limit checks now run before deep signature validation so oversized requests consistently return 413.

Validation status:
- backend: go test ./...
- All green after queue/upload hardening changes.

